. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
> ---
. * MODEL DESCRIPTION:
. * This model estimates the causal effect of having a first-born daughter on 
. * political attitudes (measured by the outcome variable `left_leaning`).
. *
. * We use the csdid command for Difference-in-Differences estimation in a 
. * repeated cross-section design, following Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021).
. * 
. * Treatment timing is defined by `first_daughter_year`, the year in which 
. * an individual first had a daughter. The outcome is observed in survey year 
. * `syear`. Never-treated individuals (those who never had a daughter) are 
. * coded with `first_daughter_year = 0`.
. *
. * Estimation uses the regression-based approach (`method(reg)`), which regres
> ses 
. * the outcome on treatment cohort × period indicators and computes group-time
>  
. * average treatment effects (ATT(g,t)).
. *
. * Identification relies on a conditional parallel trends assumption: 
. * in the absence of treatment, the outcome trajectories of treated and 
. * never-treated units would have evolved similarly, conditional on covariates
> .
. *
. * Covariates include: age, marital status, education level, income category,
. * labor force status, region (East/West Germany), and household size.
. *
. * Standard errors are clustered at the household level (`hid`).
. * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
> ---
. 
.         csdid left_leaning ///
>             i.male age i.married i.pgisced11 ///
>             i.income_cat i.labor_force_status ///
>             i.hgnuts1_ew hlk0006, ///
>             gvar(first_daughter_year) ///
>             time(syear) ///
>             method(dripw) ///
>             rseed(42) ///
>             vce(cluster hid)
Units always treated found. These will be ignored
